    "['undo portswitch', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\ndelete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `undo portswitch` command disables the switching functionality on an interface, converting it from a Layer 2 switch port to a Layer 3 routed interface. In Juniper, this is achieved by removing the `family ethernet-switching` configuration from the interface, which effectively makes it a Layer 3 interface.\\n\\nNote: I included both interface translations since they both had the `undo portswitch` command in the original configuration. If you only needed one interface translation, you would use just one of the delete commands.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\ndelete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `undo portswitch` command disables the switching functionality on an interface, converting it from a Layer 2 switch port to a Layer 3 routed interface. In Juniper, this is achieved by removing the `family ethernet-switching` configuration from the interface, which effectively makes it a Layer 3 interface.\\n\\nNote: I included both interface translations since they both had the `undo portswitch` command in the original configuration. If you only needed one interface translation, you would use just one of the delete commands.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching'}]]": 1,
