    "['undo portswitch', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\ndelete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `undo portswitch` command disables the switchport mode (Layer 2 functionality) and enables routing mode (Layer 3) on the interface. In Juniper, this is equivalent to removing the Ethernet switching configuration from the interface. \\n\\nThe Juniper commands:\\n1. Remove Ethernet switching configuration for GE1/0/0\\n2. Remove Ethernet switching configuration for GE2/0/0\\n\\nNote that Juniper interfaces are in Layer 3 mode by default when not configured for switching, so this effectively achieves the same result as Huawei's `undo portswitch`.\", 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ndelete interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\ndelete interfaces ge-2/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `undo portswitch` command disables the switchport mode (Layer 2 functionality) and enables routing mode (Layer 3) on the interface. In Juniper, this is equivalent to removing the Ethernet switching configuration from the interface. \\n\\nThe Juniper commands:\\n1. Remove Ethernet switching configuration for GE1/0/0\\n2. Remove Ethernet switching configuration for GE2/0/0\\n\\nNote that Juniper interfaces are in Layer 3 mode by default when not configured for switching, so this effectively achieves the same result as Huawei's `undo portswitch`.\", 'trans_templ